WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:02.500
FL4N: Feed-forward Latent Model for 4D Novel View Synthesis. Title card with the flan logo.

00:02.500 --> 00:06.500
Twelve frames of a monocular video fan out along a camera arc: every frame is a new viewpoint and a new instant.

00:06.500 --> 00:11.000
A view by time grid. Only the diagonal is observed. A target cell off the diagonal is rendered by FL4N.

00:11.000 --> 00:16.000
Ground truth next to four Gaussian-based baselines showing ghosting, blur, floaters and holes; FL4N's render appears with a check.

00:16.000 --> 00:25.500
The architecture figure from the paper lights up stage by stage: monocular sequence sampling, the frozen static encoder and its static latent, the dynamic encoder with learnable time tokens, static anchoring, residual latent and mask head, then the time module, sum and frozen renderer at the target view.

00:25.500 --> 00:31.500
FL4N output at a fixed novel camera while a slider sweeps time, then at a frozen instant while the camera sweeps twelve viewpoints.

00:31.500 --> 00:35.000
Three loss cards: RGB, dynamic crop and mask. Depth, optical flow and 3D motion labels are struck through.

00:35.000 --> 00:39.500
Bar charts of cross-time view synthesis PSNR on NVIDIA, N3DV and CamxTime, FL4N on top, and 40 FPS.

00:39.500 --> 00:41.500
Closing card: FL4N, latent 4D, no primitives.
